# Keep the build context small and secret-free. Everything here is either
# regenerable inside the build or has no business in an image.
#
# `target/` and `node_modules/` are the two that matter for speed: both run to
# gigabytes on a working checkout, and the whole context is packed and sent to
# the builder before the first instruction runs. `dist/` is excluded so a local
# `npm run build` can never be what ends up in the image — the Node stage builds
# the bundle itself, from the lockfile.
target/
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git/
.env
corpus/
**/*.swp

# Real config never belongs in a build context, even travelling to your own host.
rag.toml
deploy/deploy.env
